{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":46655,"duration_api_ms":48134,"ttft_ms":27561,"ttft_stream_ms":1387,"time_to_request_ms":189,"num_turns":3,"result":"{\"verdict\":\"REVISE\",\"blockers\":[\"derive_state has no terminal/closure-required signal when both revision_budget and reframe_budget are exhausted (revisions >= revision_limit and reframes >= reframe_limit): the REFRAME_REQUIRED branch only fires while reframe capacity remains, so once reframe_limit is also hit, execution falls through to the local_revisions/ADMITTED_AWAITING_PROPOSAL/NEW branches and the question is silently reported as if unrevised, hiding that policy closure is due. This must yield an explicit state (e.g. CLOSURE_REQUIRED/POLICY_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED) instead of reverting to an earlier-looking projection.\",\"append() performs no state-machine guard preventing new events (revisions, holdout reservations, additional closures) from being appended after a closure event already exists for the question; derive_state silently picks the earliest closure by (at, event_key) sort order, so a second contradictory closure (or post-closure activity) is accepted without error and only resolved by event ordering, which is fragile if 'at' values collide or clocks skew across writers.\",\"QuestionPolicy.load does not reject reframe_budget.max_per_lineage == 0 as a degenerate/disallowed configuration even though that value causes the REFRAME_REQUIRED branch to never trigger (see blocker 1); either the policy loader should require reframe_limit >= 1 or derive_state must handle the 0 case correctly.\",\"validate_event does not require holdout_final_run events to carry a run id (e.g. holdout_final_run_id) at write time, so the later closure-time check that holdout_final_run_id is present relies on the caller supplying a value that was never validated when the holdout_final_run fact itself was appended -- the referenced id could point to a run never actually recorded as a fact.\"],\"required_tests\":[\"Test that when len(revisions) >= revision_limit AND len(reframes) >= reframe_limit, derive_state returns an explicit terminal/closure-required state distinct from NEW/ADMITTED_AWAITING_PROPOSAL (currently no such assertion exists).\",\"Test appending a closure event followed by another event (e.g. proposal_revision or a second closure with a different claim) for the same question_id and assert the ledger either rejects it or derive_state's behavior is explicitly specified and covered (currently untested).\",\"Test QuestionPolicy.load with reframe_budget.max_per_lineage: 0 to confirm intended behavior (accept-and-handle vs reject at load time).\",\"Test that closure_claim == 'validated' with a holdout_final_run_id that does not correspond to any holdout_final_run event actually present in the ledger is either rejected or explicitly documented as out of scope.\",\"Test concurrent append() calls from two processes/threads with identical event content (idempotency under real lock contention, not just sequential calls) to validate the fcntl-based dedup path under race conditions.\"]}","stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"8f066dba-cf4f-47d0-abe3-874f1d665f3f","total_cost_usd":0.1567536,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14042,"cache_read_input_tokens":10682,"output_tokens":4354,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14042,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":10682,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3823,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003978,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":4354,"cacheReadInputTokens":10682,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14042,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1527756,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"verdict":"REVISE","blockers":["derive_state has no terminal/closure-required signal when both revision_budget and reframe_budget are exhausted (revisions >= revision_limit and reframes >= reframe_limit): the REFRAME_REQUIRED branch only fires while reframe capacity remains, so once reframe_limit is also hit, execution falls through to the local_revisions/ADMITTED_AWAITING_PROPOSAL/NEW branches and the question is silently reported as if unrevised, hiding that policy closure is due. This must yield an explicit state (e.g. CLOSURE_REQUIRED/POLICY_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED) instead of reverting to an earlier-looking projection.","append() performs no state-machine guard preventing new events (revisions, holdout reservations, additional closures) from being appended after a closure event already exists for the question; derive_state silently picks the earliest closure by (at, event_key) sort order, so a second contradictory closure (or post-closure activity) is accepted without error and only resolved by event ordering, which is fragile if 'at' values collide or clocks skew across writers.","QuestionPolicy.load does not reject reframe_budget.max_per_lineage == 0 as a degenerate/disallowed configuration even though that value causes the REFRAME_REQUIRED branch to never trigger (see blocker 1); either the policy loader should require reframe_limit >= 1 or derive_state must handle the 0 case correctly.","validate_event does not require holdout_final_run events to carry a run id (e.g. holdout_final_run_id) at write time, so the later closure-time check that holdout_final_run_id is present relies on the caller supplying a value that was never validated when the holdout_final_run fact itself was appended -- the referenced id could point to a run never actually recorded as a fact."],"required_tests":["Test that when len(revisions) >= revision_limit AND len(reframes) >= reframe_limit, derive_state returns an explicit terminal/closure-required state distinct from NEW/ADMITTED_AWAITING_PROPOSAL (currently no such assertion exists).","Test appending a closure event followed by another event (e.g. proposal_revision or a second closure with a different claim) for the same question_id and assert the ledger either rejects it or derive_state's behavior is explicitly specified and covered (currently untested).","Test QuestionPolicy.load with reframe_budget.max_per_lineage: 0 to confirm intended behavior (accept-and-handle vs reject at load time).","Test that closure_claim == 'validated' with a holdout_final_run_id that does not correspond to any holdout_final_run event actually present in the ledger is either rejected or explicitly documented as out of scope.","Test concurrent append() calls from two processes/threads with identical event content (idempotency under real lock contention, not just sequential calls) to validate the fcntl-based dedup path under race conditions."]},"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0f24d7d5-db91-43cd-8859-9439315d03ed"}
